# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) to point `next dev` at a deployed api.
#
# Deployed, the webapp and the api share one hostname -- the api is a second
# origin on the same CloudFront distribution, on an /api/* behavior -- so the
# browser makes no cross-origin request and there is no url to configure.
# `next dev` serves only this bundle, so next.config.ts proxies /api/* here
# and keeps that single-origin shape locally.
#
# Point it at test, not prod. Prod answers 403 to start/stop anyway (its IAM
# role has no permission for either), but GET /api/db there reports the
# production instance.
#
# Unset is fine: the page then shows a failed request, which is the truth.
DEV_API_ORIGIN=https://polaris-test.celestialstudio.net
